    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91370" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῡθιο-νίκης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span></span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῡθιό-ᾱς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>conqueror in the Pythian
			games</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				3.1178.67
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				5.19
			</span></i>:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῡθιο-νίκη</span></b> , ἡ, pr.n. of a
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταίρα</span>, afterwards deified as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Π. Ἀφροδίτη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Python
				1.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				26.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Timocl.
				17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Hist.
				244
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				245
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.37.2
			</span></i>; called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πυθονίκη</span></b> 
			in <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				17.108
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Phoc.</u>
				22
			</span></i> (so, of another woman, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.3823
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πυθιονίκη</span>
			=
			<i>Pythian victory</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				5.19
			</span></i>.</div>
